# Root-level prettier ignore. Each package already has its own `.prettierignore`
# for `pnpm -r lint`; this one governs `lint:root`, which checks the repo root
# and `port/*.md` — the documents no package-scoped gate ever reached.

# Vendored dependencies. Never ours to format.
node_modules

# The upstream Astryx clone, cloned read-only as porting reference. Its prose
# and code are Meta's, not this port's, and reformatting it would just be
# unreviewable diff noise against a tree we don't own.
reference

# Imported historical prose (one file per shipped batch). Provably does not
# converge under `prettier --write` — a multi-paragraph list item gets its
# continuation paragraphs re-indented deeper on every pass (6 -> 10 -> ... ->
# 30 spaces observed), which past ~4 extra spaces renders as an indented code
# block in GFM. That is silent content corruption, not a formatting nit, so
# the ledger is excluded rather than rewritten to fit the gate.
port/ledger

# SvelteKit's generated build output for the docs site.
docs/.svelte-kit

# `svelte-package` output for every publishable package. Built artifacts, not
# source — and `packages/core/dist/**/*.stylex.js` ships deliberately
# uncompiled (see CLAUDE.md), so it is not representative source to format.
packages/*/dist
